The '''Porciúncula–Jatiel high-speed rail line''', alternatively known as the '''''Direto''''', is a {{convert|936.79|km|adj=on}} {{W|standard gauge}} {{W|railway line}} inaugurated on 9 April 1969, becoming the inaugural [[AVB|AVB rail line]] in Balisca. Designed for speeds up to {{convert|360|km/h|mph|0|abbr=on}} and compatibility with neighboring countries' rail systems, it connects the cities of [[Porciúncula]], [[Calatañazor]], [[Castejón]], [[Yerba Buena]] and [[Jatiel]] in 2 hours 30 minutes. 

In Jatiel, the line merges into the [[Daramazán–Jatiel high speed rail line]]. Along with being one of the world's oldest high-speed rail lines, it is also one of the most heavily used.

Trains are operated by the confederal [[Baliscan Railways Group]] as part of the the [[AVB]] service.

